# Multi-Profile Google OAuth Token Paths

Discovered during session on 2026-06-17.

## Token Locations

Two parallel storage locations exist:

1. **Primary (secrets)**: `/opt/data/secrets/google/tokens/<profile>/google_token.json`
   - Used by the Google Workspace skill when `HERMES_HOME` points to the profile directory.
   - Profiles: `personal-main`, `personal-secondary`, `hermes-agent`, `burner`, `classicalechos`, `fareed320` (symlink to personal-secondary), `trapiistan`.

2. **Profile registry**: `/opt/data/google_profiles/<profile>/google_token.json`
   - Created by the setup script when `HERMES_HOME` is set to `/opt/data/google_profiles/<profile>`.
   - Contains `google_client_secret.json` and `google_oauth_pending.json` during OAuth flow.

## Usage Pattern

To operate on a specific profile, set `HERMES_HOME` before running the setup or API scripts:

```bash
HERMES_HOME=/opt/data/google_profiles/fareed320 python3 /opt/data/skills/productivity/google-workspace/scripts/setup.py --auth-url
```

The `_hermes_home.py` module resolves `HERMES_HOME` from environment variable, falling back to `~/.hermes`.

## OAuth Flow for fareed320 (personal-secondary)

- Client secret: `/opt/data/google_profiles/fareed320/google_client_secret.json`
- Token target: `/opt/data/google_profiles/fareed320/google_token.json` (will be created after auth)
- Pending state stored in `/opt/data/google_profiles/fareed320/google_oauth_pending.json`

After successful auth, the token should be copied/synced to `/opt/data/secrets/google/tokens/personal-secondary/google_token.json` for consistency.

## Scope Requirements for Newsletter Processing

Required scopes for reading and deleting emails:
- `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly`
- `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.modify`
- `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send` (if sending replies)

These are already included in the full Workspace scope set.